            <ArticleTitle>Periaortitis heralding Wegener's granulomatosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>392-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a 47-year-old man who successively presented atheromatous coronary artery disease, cholesterol embolism after angioplasty, periaortitis with presence of c-ANCA, and finally typical pulmonary lesions caused by Wegener's granulomatosis. This case illustrates the link between atheromatous and inflammatory process and emphasizes that periaortitis may be a feature of Wegener's granulomatosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
